sum='Daadi (grandmother) writes a letter to her grandchildren Vikram and Vaibhavi, happy that they are better after using her natural cures. She learnt these cures from her own grandmother, who found remedies in the kitchen for weather-related illnesses. She explains: turmeric (haldi) improves energy and digestion and reduces body pain; fenugreek (methi) seeds soaked overnight – the water drunk in the morning – help control sugar level and body weight; cumin (jeera) water improves digestion and helps sleeplessness; asafoetida (heeng) water on a baby’s tummy relieves gas and it helps control cough and cold; cinnamon (dalchini) and clove (laung) relieve toothache until we see a dentist; ginger (adrak) helps with cough, cold and pain and has been used in cooking for over 4000 years; black pepper (kali mirch) helps digestion and body pain; fennel (saunf) and carom (ajwain) after meals help digestion; cardamom (elaichi) helps digestion, breathing troubles and bad breath. She asks them to identify these spices in the kitchen and to always consult an elder before using them.',
